  <title>Images</title>

  <p><gui>+ Image</gui> asks for a JPEG or PNG file and puts it on the label.
  Dragged onto the canvas, it asks once you let go, and the image lands
  there.</p>

  <p>A thermal printer prints only black dots, so the image is resized to its
  box and turned into a pattern of black and white dots. What the canvas
  shows is that pattern: exactly what is saved in the file and sent to the
  printer. Resizing the image makes the pattern again from the original
  file, at the new size, so it never blurs from being resized twice.</p>

  <p>To use another file in the same place and size, select the image and
  press <gui>Replace Image…</gui> in the Properties panel.</p>

  <note>
    <p>White parts of an image are not white ink; they are simply not
    printed. Anything beneath an image prints through its white parts, and
    the canvas shows that. To keep something beneath from printing, clear
    its <gui>Print This Element</gui>.</p>
  </note>

  <p>The picture is kept inside the label file. A logo used on many labels
  can be stored on the printer once instead: see
  <link xref="stored-graphics"/>.</p>
</page>
